    "assetCatalog": {
      "Ability§A Plan Generations in the Making": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "At the end of your Command phase, if this unit is within range of an objective marker you control, that objective marker remains under your control, even if you have no models within range of it, until your opponent controls it at the start or end of any turn."
      },
      "Ability§Battlefield Analysis": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Once per turn, you can select one model or unit from your army with this ability as the target of a Stratagem. If it does, reduce the CP cost of that use of that Stratagem by 1CP."
      },
      "Ability§Bio-horror Disruption (psychic)": {
        "text": "While this model is leading a unit, ranged weapons equipped by models in that unit have the [LETHAL HITS] ability."
      },
      "Ability§Biological Warfare": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Oncer per battle, when this model’s unit is selected to fight, this model can use this ability. If it does, until the end of the phase, improve the Attacks and Damage characteristics of its injector goad by 3."
      },
      "Ability§Bodyguard": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While this model is leading a unit, other Character models attached to that unit have the Feel No Pain 4+ ability."
      },
      "Ability§Brood Surge": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time an enemy unit is selected to shoot, after that unit has shot, if any models from this unit were destroyed as a result of those attacks, this unit can make a Brood Surge move. To do so, roll one D6: this unit can be moved a number of inches up to the result, but it must end that move as close as possible to the closest enemy unit (excluding **Aircraft**). When doing so, those models can be moved within Engagement Range of that enemy unit.\n\nIf, at the start of the battle, no model in this unit is equipped with a hand flamer, each time this unit makes a Brood Surge move, it can be moved up to 6\" instead of up to D6\". A unit cannot make a Brood Surge move while it is Battle-shocked."
      },
      "Ability§Claimed for the Cult": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "At the start of your Command phase, roll one D6 for each objective marker you control that has one or more units from your army with this ability within range of it. If one or more of the results is a 4+, you gain 1CP."
      },
      "Ability§Cloaked Assassin": {
        "text": "If this model is equipped with a Sanctus bio-dagger, enemy units cannot use the Fire Overwatch Stratagem to shoot at this model."
      },
      "Ability§Cosmic Horror (psychic)": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "At the start of the Fight phase, each enemy unit within 6″ of this model must take a Battle-shock test."
      },
      "Ability§Creeping Shadow": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "If this model is equipped a cult sniper rifle, once per turn, when an enemy unit ends a Normal, Advance or Fall Back move within 9\" of this mode, if this model is not within Engagement Range of one or more enemy units, it can make a Normal move of up to 6\"."
      },
      "Ability§Crossfire": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, after this unit has shot, select one enemy unit hit by one or more of those attacks. Until the end of the turn, each time a friendly **Genestealer Cults** unit makes an attack that targets that enemy unit, improve the Armour Penetration characteristic of that attack by 1. The same enemy unit can only be affected by this ability once per turn."
      },
      "Ability§Cult Ambush": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Faction"
          ]
        },
        "text": "If your Army Faction is Genestealer Cults, you start the battle with a number of Resurgence points, depending on the battle size, as shown below.\n\n ■ Incursion: 6 Resurgence points\n\n ■ Strike Force: 10 Resurgence points\n\n ■ Onslaught: 14 Resurgence points\n\nEach time a unit from your army is destroyed, if every model in that unit has this ability, you can spend the relevant number of Resurgence points shown below based on that unit’s Starting Strength.\n\nAberrants\n- 5 models ....................................................... 4 Resurgence points\n- 10 models .................................................... 8 Resurgence points\n\nAcolyte Hybrids with Autopistols, Acolyte Hybrids with \nHand Flamers, Hybrid Metamorphs\n- 5 models ....................................................... 2 Resurgence points\n- 10 models .................................................... 4 Resurgence points\n\nAtalan Jackals\n- 5 models ....................................................... 2 Resurgence points\n- 10 models .................................................... 6 Resurgence points\n\nNeophyte Hybrids\n- 10 models .................................................... 3 Resurgence points\n- 20 models ................................................... 6 Resurgence points\n\nPurestrain Genestealers\n- 5 models ....................................................... 2 Resurgence points\n- 10 models .................................................... 6 Resurgence points\n\nIf you do:\n\n■ Add a new unit to your army identical to your destroyed unit, in Cult Ambush, at its Starting Strength, with all of its wounds remaining and any \n[ONE SHOT] weapons those models are equipped with considered as not having been shot.\n\n■ Place one Cult Ambush marker (see below) anywhere on the battlefield that is more than 9\" horizontally away from all enemy units (if this is not \npossible, no marker is placed).\n\n**UNITS IN CULT AMBUSH**\n\nCult Ambush is a type of Strategic Reserves. Units in Cult Ambush cannot be targeted with the Rapid Ingress Stratagem, but can be set up on the battlefield using a Cult Ambush marker as described below, or by following the rules for Strategic Reserves in a subsequent turn.\n\n**CULT AMBUSH MARKERS**\n\nUse a circular 32mm diameter marker for Cult Ambush markers. If an enemy model (excluding Aircraft) ends any kind of move within 9\" of a Cult Ambush marker you placed, that Cult Ambush marker is removed from the battlefield. At the end of the Reinforcements step of your opponent’s next Movement phase, for each of your Cult Ambush markers still on the battlefield, you can select one unit from your army that is in Cult Ambush and set up that unit using that Cult Ambush marker. To do so, set that unit up on the battlefield more than 9\" horizontally away from all enemy units, with at least one model in that unit touching that Cult Ambush marker and all other models placed wholly within 3\" of that Cult Ambush marker (that Cult Ambush marker is then removed from the battlefield)."
      },
      "Ability§Cult Demagogue": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While this model is leading a unit, each time a model in that unit makes an attack, you\ncan add 1 to the Hit roll."
      },
      "Ability§Cult Infiltration": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "At the start of each player’s Command phase, if this model is on the battlefield, you can select one of your Cult Ambush markers that is in the battlefield and has not been moved this turn and move it up to 6\"."
      },
      "Ability§Decoys and Misdirection": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "If your army includes one or more models with this ability, after both players have deployed their armies, select up to three Genestealer Cults units from your army and redeploy them. When doing so, you can set those units up in Strategic Reserves if you wish, regardless of how many units are already in Strategic Reserves."
      },
      "Ability§Demolition Run": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Once per turn, in your Movement phase, when this unit ends a Normal, Advance or Fall Back move, you can select one enemy unit within 6\" of and visible to this unit and roll one D6 for each *Atalan Jackals* model in this unit: for each 4+, that enemy unit suffers 1 mortal wound (to a maximum of 6 mortal wounds)."
      },
      "Ability§Fire Support": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "removed": {
          "text": ""
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, after this model has shot, select one enemy unit it scored one or more hits against this phase. Until the end of the phase, each time a friendly model that disembarked from this Transport this turn makes an attack that targets that enemy unit, you can re-roll the Wound roll."
      },
      "Ability§Grinding Line-breaker": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time an enemy unit (excluding **Monsters** or **Vehicles**) that is within Engagement Range of this model Falls Back, all models in that enemy unit must take a Desperate Escape test. When doing so, if that enemy unit is Battle-shocked, subtract 1 from each of those tests."
      },
      "Ability§Heroic Fusilade": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Once per turn, after one model from your army with this ability has shot, you can select one **Infantry** unit hit by one or more of those attacks. That unit must take a Battle-shock test."
      },
      "Ability§Hulking Bodyguards": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While a Character is leading this unit, each time an attack targets this unit, if the Strength characteristic of that attack is greater than the Toughness characteristic of this unit, subtract 1 from the Wound roll."
      },
      "Ability§Hypersensory Abilities": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Once per turn, in your opponent's Movement phase, when an enemy unit ends a Normal, Advance or Fall Back move within 9\" of this model, if this model is not within Engagement Range of one or more enemy units, it can shoot at that unit as if it were your Shooting phase and then make a Normal move of up to D6 (it cannot embark within a **Transport** as part of this move)."
      },
      "Ability§Industrialised Destruction": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time a model in this unit makes an attack, re-roll a Wound roll of 1. If the target of that attack is an enemy unit within range of an objective marker, you can re-roll the Wound roll."
      },
      "Ability§Manufactorum Cover": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time a ranged attack is allocated to a model, if that model is not fully visible to every model in the attacking unit because of this Fortification, that model has the Benefit of Cover against that attack."
      },
      "Ability§Master Outrider": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, after this model’s unit has shot, if it is not within Engagement Range of any enemy units, that unit can make a Normal move of up to 6″ as if it were your Movement phase. If it does, until the end of the turn, that unit is not eligible to declare a charge."
      },
      "Ability§Might From Beyond": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While this model is leading a unit, melee weapons equipped by models in that unit have the [DEVASTATING WOUNDS] ability."
      },
      "Ability§Mind Control (psychic)": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "At the start of your opponent’s Shooting phase, one Psyker model from your army with this ability can use it. If used, select one enemy unit within 18″ of that Psyker model and roll one D6: on a 1, that Psyker model suffers D3 mortal wounds; on a 2-5, until the end of the phase, each time a model in that enemy unit makes an attack, subtract 1 from the Hit roll; on a 6, each time a model in that unit makes an attack, subtract 1 from the Hit roll and subtract 1 from the Wound roll."
      },
      "Ability§Nexus of Devotion": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While this model is leading a unit, models in that unit have the Feel No Pain 5+ ability. If that unit has the **Hybrid Metamorphs** keyword, models in that unit have the Feel No Pain 4+ ability instead."
      },
      "Ability§One Shot": {
        "text": "The bearer can only shoot with this weapon once per battle."
      },
      "Ability§Outrider Gangs": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time you use the Cult Ambush ability to set this unit back up on the battlefield, in addition to the normal rules, all of its models must be set up wholly within 9″ of a battlefield edge and at least one of its models must be touching one of your Cult Ambush markers (that marker is then removed from the battlefield). If this cannot be done, this unit cannot be set back up."
      },
      "Ability§Planted Explosives": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Once per battle, when an enemy unit ends a Normal, Advance or Fall Back move within 9″ of this model, this model can use its Reductus mine. If it does, roll one D6: on a 2+, that enemy unit suffers D3+3 mortal wounds. Only one model from your army with this ability can use it in the same battle round. \n\n**Designer’s Note**: Place a Reductus Mine token next to the model, removing it once this ability has been used."
      },
      "Ability§Primed and Ready": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "removed": {
          "text": ""
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, you can select one model from your army with this ability as the target of the Grenade Stratagem for 0CP, provided that model has not already been the target of that Stratagem this phase. This can allow you to use the Grenade Stratagem for a second time this phase."
      },
      "Ability§Primed and Ready (Reductus)": {
        "aspects": {
          "Label": "Prime and Ready"
        },
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "removed": {
          "text": ""
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, you can select one model from your army with this ability as the target of the Grenade Stratagem for 0CP, provided that model has not already been the target of that Stratagem this phase."
      },
      "Ability§Priority Target": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Shooting phase, after this model's unit has shot, select one enemy unit hit by one or more of those attacks made with a cult sniper rifle. Until the end of the phase, each time a friendly **Genestealer Cults** model makes an attack that targets that enemy unit, re-roll a Hit roll of 1."
      },
      "Ability§Psionic Shield (psychic)": {
        "text": "Once per battle, at the start of any phase, this model can use this ability. If it does, until the end of the phase, this model has a 4+ invulnerable save."
      },
      "Ability§Psychic Familiar": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Once per battle, at the start of the Fight phase, this model can use its psychic familiar. If it does, until the end of the phase, add 6\" to the range of its Cosmic Horror ability. \n\nDesigner’s Note: Place a Psychic Familiar token next to the model, removing it once this ability has been used."
      },
      "Ability§Psychic Familiar (Magus)": {
        "aspects": {
          "Label": "Psychic Familiar"
        },
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Once per battle, at the start of your opponent's Shooting phase, this model can use its psychic familiar. If it does, until the end of phase, add 6\" to the range of its Mind Control ability."
      },
      "Ability§Psychic Spoor": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "At the start of the first battle round, select one enemy unit to be this model’s prey. Each time this model makes an attack that targets its prey, you can re-roll the Hit roll and you can re-roll the Wound roll."
      },
      "Ability§Regenerating Gene-mass": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "The first time this model is destroyed, roll one D6 at the end of the phase. On a 2+, set this model back up on the battlefield as close as possible to where it was destroyed and not within Engagement Range of any enemy units, with its full wounds remaining."
      },
      "Ability§Scrambler Array": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Enemy units that are set up on the battlefield as Reinforcements cannot be set up within 12″ of this model."
      },
      "Ability§Spiritual Leader": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Once per battle, at the start of any phase, you can select one friendly **Genestealer Cults** unit that is Battle-shocked and within 12\" of tihs model. That unit is no longer Battle-shocked."
      },
      "Ability§Sudden Assault": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While this model is leading a unit, models in that unit have the Fights First ability."
      },
      "Ability§Summon the Cult": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Once per battle, when you have to remove a Cult Ambush marker because your opponent has moved too close to it, if one or more models from your army with this ability are on the battlefield, you can use this ability. If you do, instead of removing that marker, you can place it anywhere on the battlefield that is within 12″ of a model from your army with this ability and more than 9″ horizontally away from all enemy units (if this is not possible, this ability is not considered to have been used and that marker is removed as normal)."
      },
      "Ability§Supreme Commander": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": []
        },
        "text": ""
      },
      "Ability§Supreme Commander (Patriarch)": {
        "aspects": {
          "Label": "Supreme Commander"
        },
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": []
        },
        "rules": {
          "setWarlord": {
            "actions": [
              {
                "actionType": "set",
                "iterations": 1,
                "paths": [
                  [
                    "{parent}",
                    "stats",
                    "Warlord",
                    "value"
                  ]
                ],
                "value": "✓"
              }
            ],
            "evals": [],
            "evaluate": "AND",
            "failState": "pass",
            "order": 20
          }
        },
        "text": "* You cannot include more than one **Patriarch** model in your army.\n* If this model is in your army, it must be your **Warlord**."
      },
      "Ability§Swift and Deadly": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "This unit is eligible to declare a charge in a turn in which it Advanced."
      },
      "Ability§Tectonic Fragdrill": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Friendly Genestealer Cult Infantry models can be set up or end any type of move on top of the floor sections of this Fortification."
      },
      "Ability§The Chosen One": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While this model is leading a unit, each time a model in that unit is destroyed by a melee attack, if that model has not fought this phase, roll one D6. On a 4+, do not remove the destroyed model from play; it can fight after the attacking model's unit has finished making attacks, and is then removed from play."
      },
      "Ability§Twisted Science": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While this model is leading a unit, melee weapons equipped by models in that unit have the [LETHAL HITS] ability."
      },
      "Ability§Underground Egress": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time one of your Cult Ambush markers is removed as the result of an enemy unit ending any kind of move within 9″ of it, you can instead move that marker so that it is wholly within 9″ of this Fortification and more than 9″ horizontally away from all enemy units (if this is not possible, that marker is removed as normal)."
      },
      "Ability§Voice of New Truths": {
        "keywords": {
          "Keywords": [
            "Other"
          ]
        },
        "text": "In your Command phase, one model from your army with this ability can use it. If it does, select one enemy unit within 18\" of it, that unit must take a Batlte-shock test."
      },
      "Battle Trait§Alien Resilience": {
