      "Ability§World: Hive World": {
        "text": "Institutions: Community, Industry, Politics. Ascension reward — Strength of the Masses: After each Crusade battle, each BATTLELINE unit that was part of your Crusade army and survived the battle gains 1XP."
      },
      "Ability§World: Forge World": {
        "text": "Institutions: Industry, Military, Religion. Ascension reward — Prized Acquisition: Each time you add a VEHICLE unit to your Order of Battle, that unit gains 6XP (and therefore gains the Blooded Rank); select one Battle Honour for it as normal."
      },
      "Ability§World: Cardinal World": {
        "text": "Institutions: Community, Politics, Religion. Ascension reward — Will of the Faithful: After each Crusade battle, you can ignore your first failed Out of Action test."
      },
      "Ability§World: Fortress World": {
        "text": "Institutions: Military, Religion, Resources. Ascension reward — Looted Armoury: When a unit from your Crusade force gains the Weapon Modifications Battle Honour, you can roll 3D6 (instead of 2D6) to randomly determine three Weapon Modifications for the weapon to gain."
      },
      "Ability§World: Agri/Mining World": {
        "text": "Institutions: Community, Industry, Resources. Ascension reward — Hard Graft: After each Crusade battle, roll one D6: on a 4+, you gain 1 additional Requisition point."
      },
      "Ability§World: Frontier/Feudal World": {
        "text": "Institutions: Military, Politics, Resources. Ascension reward — Cult of Personality: Each time you select a unit to be Marked for Greatness, that unit gains 1 additional XP."
      },
      "Institution§Institution 1": {
        "text": "Controlled Institution benefits: **Industry:** Use the Rearm and Resupply Requisition up to two times without spending any Requisition points. **Military:** One INFANTRY unit (excluding CHARACTER units) with fewer than 6XP gains XP until it has 6XP. **Community:** Use the Fresh Recruits Requisition up to two times without spending any Requisition points. **Politics:** You gain influence. While you have influence, subtract 1 from your next Setback roll, then you no longer have influence. **Religion:** One CHARACTER unit with fewer than 6XP gains XP until it has 6XP. **Resources:** Use the Increase Supply Limit Requisition up to two times without spending any Requisition points."
      },
      "Institution§Institution 2": {
        "text": "See Institution 1 for the Controlled Institution benefits."
      },
      "Institution§Institution 3": {
        "text": "See Institution 1 for the Controlled Institution benefits."
      },
      "Path of Ascension§Path of Ascension": {
        "assets": {
          "traits": [
            "Institution§Institution 1",
            "Institution§Institution 2",
            "Institution§Institution 3"
          ]
        },
        "text": "**Path of Ascension.** If your Crusade force includes a PATRIARCH, PRIMUS or MAGUS and is not on a Path, it can begin one: pick or roll the world classification (D6 1–6 in the order listed), choose which of its three institutions your uprising has infiltrated, name the world. Before each battle, if you do not already control three institutions, select a target institution you do not control.\n\n**After each battle:** Exploit Advantage (if the target is infiltrated, each surviving unit of your army gains 1XP) → Gain Ascension Points (D6, +1 won, +1 target infiltrated, +1 a unit earned XP from a Genestealer Cults Agenda: 4–7 = 1 point, 8+ = 2) → Gain Control (at 3 Ascension points spend them: Control +1, the target becomes Controlled; at Control 4 you win a Glorious Ascension; otherwise take the institution's benefit or 1RP) → Setback (2D6, +1 lost, +1 no Agenda XP, +Control: on 13+ you are set back and must fight the Great Ordeal) → Propagate (optional: D6 + Control, on 5+ Propagation +1 and Control −1; at Propagation 5 you win Seed the Stars).\n\n**Path's End.** Glorious Ascension: one PATRIARCH gains 2XP and you claim the world's Ascension reward. Seed the Stars: up to three CHARACTERS gain 2XP. The Great Ordeal: a battle with Zealous Fury (+Control to your Battle-shock tests) and Persecuted (your opponent starts with CP by battle size and your Control: Combat Patrol 1/1/0/0, Incursion 2/1/1/0, Strike Force 3/2/1/1, Onslaught 3/3/2/1 for Control 0/1/2/3; Prepared for the Ordeal gives you 2CP); win it for 2XP on a PATRIARCH and the Ascension reward, lose it and you must abandon the Path. Abandoning (The Cycle Begins Anew) costs an Ignominy: every PATRIARCH, PRIMUS and MAGUS gains a Battle Scar, or you remove one Ascension reward. Each ending resets Ascension points, Propagation and Control to 0; after a victory your next Path starts with two infiltrated institutions.\n\nEach Ascension reward claimed adds 1 to your Crusade points when determining Crusade Blessings."
      }
    },
